# A conversation that quotes a picture or clip marker -- a pasted chat template, a log, this server's own
# refusal -- used to end every turn that also carried a real picture: the frontend counted the quoted markers as
# media ('the prompt's image and video markers do not match its images and videos'), and since the quotation sits
# in the history, the refusal then repeated forever. A real session carried 59 of them. A quoted marker cannot be
# told from a marker the template wrote -- they are the same bytes -- so server/prompts.py now marks every picture
# and clip of a request (not only tool results') with a per-request nonce rendered before its marker, and the
# frontend's escape_quoted neutralizes every marker that does not stand behind one: a quotation stays text (a
# zero-width space after '<|'), the request's own markers still expand, and a template or client that drops a
# picture still refuses. A bare mention is escaped the same way. Speed is untouched: prompt preparation, once a
# request, and only for one that carries media (prose decode measured 62.6-65.9 tok/s, floor 60). Applies after
# 0074-glm-picture-cache.patch. Apache-2.0.

